From 39fb79e11e3479cd6cf9351ede928b535c3c234c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 15:39:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Mission tick no longer rides on the Game, and F12 says what
 is true

I have now guessed at this twice and been wrong twice, so this stops guessing.

The tick was reached through Game.mission_index, set by GameInitBox when it
starts a mission. Every reading of that path says it should work, and it plainly
does not, so the dependency is removed rather than defended: the start screen now
records what it launched in a global of its own, and a finished game ticks off
whichever index is available - the Game's if it has one (which keeps a mission
resumed from a save correct), otherwise the launcher's. Nothing that copies,
resets or re-creates the Game between starting and winning can lose it now.
Starting a custom game clears it, so a custom game cannot tick off a mission.

To make the remaining possibilities distinguishable rather than inferred:

- F12 now also dumps the progress state - where the ini is and whether it
  exists, what the start screen last launched, this game's mission_index,
  game_over and game_over_shown, which index a win would tick, and every
  mission currently recorded complete.

- The write reads itself straight back and says so. "Never called" and "called
  but did not persist" look identical from the start screen, and telling them
  apart is most of the remaining work.

No behaviour changes beyond the fallback; the rest is instrumentation.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
